# Memory architecture audit — elaborated inventory (F5/F7, RUN-0009).
#
#   node scripts/eda/audit_memory.js --elaborate
#
# Run it through that wrapper, not directly: this script writes into
# build/asic_evidence/memory_audit/, and the Yosys build in use has no
# `file mkdir`, so a direct run on a clean checkout fails with
# "ERROR: Can't create file ...". The wrapper creates the directory, runs this
# script and then the checker.
#
# Reads the same file list as fullsoc_map.ys, elaborates `has_soc`, lowers
# processes and collects memory cells, then writes the inventory BEFORE any
# mapping. No techmap, no flatten: this script answers "which memories exist and
# how big are they", not "what do they map to".
#
# Outputs (evidence, not inputs):
#   build/asic_evidence/memory_audit/memory_cells.json   stat -json per module
#   build/asic_evidence/memory_audit/memories.il         RTLIL with $mem_v2
#                                                        parameters (SIZE, WIDTH,
#                                                        ABITS, RD/WR ports)
#
# The RTLIL file is the authoritative geometry source parsed by
# scripts/eda/audit_memory.js. `stat` alone only counts memories, it does not
# expose SIZE/WIDTH, and the older "3 memories" note came from counting.

read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/reset_ctrl.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/axi_lite_interconnect.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/axi_lite_to_apb.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/boot_rom.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/has_addr_map.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/intc_axi.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/req_gnt_to_axi_lite.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/watchdog.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/plic.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/clint.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/debug_jtag.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/power_mgr.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/i2c_ctrl.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/spi_ctrl.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/power_mgr_regs.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/i2s.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/gpio.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/timer.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/pwm.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/uart.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_peripherals/qspi_flash_ctrl.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/riscv_core.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/sram.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/rtl_top/has_soc.sv

hierarchy -check -top has_soc

# Processes must be lowered before memories can be collected.
proc
memory_collect
opt_clean

# Inventory first, assertions after: the evidence must exist even if a later
# step fails.
tee -o build/asic_evidence/memory_audit/memory_cells.json stat -json
write_rtlil build/asic_evidence/memory_audit/memories.il
